  "worked_solution": "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+P(x){y}^{\u2032}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{\u2032}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{\u2032}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{\u2032}(x) & =-{e}^{x}W(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
